    {
      "entry_id": "ao-mixed-operator",
      "subject": "AO_Mixed virtual map: baked AO mesh map combined with the AO channel",
      "status": "calibrated",
      "formula": "AO_Mixed = a * c, the product (multiply) of the baked AO mesh map value a and the AO channel value c, both linear in [0, 1] (a = mesh map code / 65535, c = stored L16 code / 65535; no colour transfer). The result is written at 8-bit precision: v = a * c is truncated to 12 fractional bits (j = floor(v * 4096)), then code8 = floor((j * 255 + 2047) / 4096), the nearest 8-bit code with ties down; the PNG 16 export writes code8 * 257. An AO channel with no layer stores its base 1.0 (code 65535), so AO_Mixed equals the mesh map quantised to 8 bits. No clamp is needed (a * c is in [0, 1]).",
      "public_sources": [
        {
          "source_id": "A-HELP-EXPORT",
          "locator": "Output templates: virtual maps, Mixed AO"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "A-PYDOC",
          "locator": "textureset: MeshMapUsage.AO; ChannelType.AO"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "X-D3D12",
          "locator": "Data conversion rules: FLOAT to UNORM"
        }
      ],
