      "notes": "Whole image (one quad per set, full 0-1 UVs). min(a, c) misses by up to 16448 export codes; a 16-bit product misses by up to 145. Every recorded AO_Mixed value is on the 8-bit lattice (multiple of 257). Plain round-to-nearest of 255 * a * c leaves 2060 (s0) and about 2400 (s1) values one 8-bit code high, all at fractions 0.50-0.56; the 12-bit truncation removes them (the same n + 4 bit truncation fits the 16-bit normal maps, height-to-normal.json). s0, s2 and s3 are exact against both recordings. s1 (fill at opacity 0.5) leaves 30 (r1) and 17 (r2) values one 8-bit code (257) off, every one within 0.03 of a 2^-12 step; the oracle is unstable on the same values (r1 and r2 differ in 27 values, max 257, all within 0.03 of a step), so an exact fit against both recordings is impossible there. Using the unquantised blend 0.5 + 0.5 * b in place of the stored L16 channel fits worse (29 and 50 values)."
    },
